  "Notes": [
    "Self-contained input. Every pressure is absolute Pa; velocities are interstitial at the specified source pressure and temperature.",
    "Adsorption feed and cold HTF reference are 298.15 K; nonisothermal bed temperatures are solved.",
    "Original two-site fit order and full workbook precision are retained; no mixture refit. SEI is not SCI or IAST.",
    "Kinetics, transport, pellet density and hardware are common screening assumptions, not measured material properties.",
    "The energy equation uses the 298.15 K Henry-limit-weighted constant heat from the supplied site fits; equilibrium retains both individual site heats.",
    "Light purge uses remembered product composition and is subtracted from net product. Pure-CH4 fallback is startup only; a finite product tank is not modelled.",
    "Two-column CSS compares a complete schedule with both A/B role exchanges; total adsorbent mass is used for productivity.",
    "ADS, pressure, purge and PE durations are fixed. ADS has no composition stopping rule.",
    "HEAT stops on the coldest solid node >=375 K; COOL on the warmest gas/solid/wall node <=300 K. A timeout advances diagnostically and excludes the reporting window from ranking.",
    "Purge flow is 0.10 of ADS flow; the fixed purge duration is derived to give 0.10 mol purge per mol preceding ADS feed.",
    "Initial gas composition basis is feed, with equilibrium loading. Startup is excluded only after CSS is established.",
    "All ADS, repressurization and cooling fresh feed is tagged separately and totalled. Recovery includes all external fresh inlet methane, excluding internal recycle.",
    "Plant capacity is 1000 Nm3/h cycle-average tagged fresh feed, including all scheduled waiting time. It is not the product target.",
    "The light receiver retains the original feed-composition backflow assumption; timed ADS removes the premature-stop trigger but does not correct receiver physics.",
    "This is a screening recipe, not an optimized cycle, calibrated process or completed TEA. Fixed-cycle completion is not CSS."
  ],
